  "note": "Triennial borough election: nomination day 4 May, polling day (had there been contests) 18 May 1949 (Belfast News-Letter, 4 and 18 May 1949, p. 5). \"All twelve vacancies for Councillors were filled by the unopposed return of twelve nominees of the Portadown Unionist Association\"; ten were members of the outgoing council, and James Finlay (a former urban councillor) and Charles Cooper were new. The three aldermen elected in 1947 were not due for election."
